WEBVTT

NOTE
This file was generated by Descript <www.descript.com>

00:00:00.970 --> 00:00:04.900
Rhiannon: Person-centred care with
Children and young people, means that they

00:00:04.940 --> 00:00:06.880
are at the centre of the support offered.

00:00:07.430 --> 00:00:12.070
That support includes choice and is
holistic and specifically tailored to

00:00:12.070 --> 00:00:13.890
the young person’s needs and wishes.

00:00:17.070 --> 00:00:20.439
In the past, people were expected
to fit in with the routines and

00:00:20.440 --> 00:00:24.230
practices that health and social
services felt were most appropriate.

00:00:25.060 --> 00:00:29.070
But in order to be person-centred,
services have had to change to be

00:00:29.070 --> 00:00:33.100
more flexible to meet individual needs
in a manner that is best for them.

00:00:34.350 --> 00:00:37.839
Leah: Being compassionate, thinking about
things from the person’s point of view

00:00:38.240 --> 00:00:40.610
and being respectful are all important.

00:00:41.060 --> 00:00:43.629
This might be shown through sharing
decisions with a young person

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:46.690
and their family and helping
them to manage their health.

00:00:47.719 --> 00:00:51.270
It is as much about the way
professionals and individuals think

00:00:51.280 --> 00:00:55.250
about care and their relationships,
then the actual services available.

00:00:56.130 --> 00:01:00.010
Rhiannon: There are also different ways
this partnership can work, such as on

00:01:00.010 --> 00:01:04.419
a one-to-one basis, where children and
young people take part in decisions about

00:01:04.420 --> 00:01:11.850
their health and care directly, or on a
collective group basis, whereby groups

00:01:11.889 --> 00:01:16.410
are involved in decisions about the design
and delivery of person centred services.

00:01:19.850 --> 00:01:23.400
The underlying philosophy is the
same, it is all about doing things

00:01:23.410 --> 00:01:25.599
with people, rather than ‘to’ them.

00:01:26.440 --> 00:01:29.730
Leah: Including young people in the
decision making around their mental

00:01:29.730 --> 00:01:34.000
health care leads to better involvement
and engagement and can help in

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:36.220
creating a successful recovery model.

